  data: {
    LLM: "Game: Domino Loo. 2-4 players, double-six dominoes (28 tiles). Deal 5 each, turn up 1 for trumps (higher end = trump suit). Can swap for The Miss widow hand or drop out. Dealer may swap one tile for turn-up. 5 tricks. Must follow suit; must trump if void. Each trick = 1/5 of pool. Zero tricks = 'Looed' (penalty = pool amount).",
    Player: "Welcome to Domino Loo! I'll deal you 5 tiles and turn up one to set trumps. You can keep your hand, swap for The Miss (a mystery widow hand), or drop out. Win tricks to earn pool sharesâ€”but win zero tricks and you're 'Looed', paying a penalty! Follow suit if you can, trump if you can't. Dealer gets to swap for the turn-up trump tile.",
    objective: "Win as many tricks as possible to take a share of the pool. Avoid being 'Looed' (taking zero tricks).",
    gameplay: "1. **Trumps**: The higher end of the turn-up tile is the trump suit. 2. **The Miss (Widow)**: In 3-4 player games, an extra hand of 5 tiles is dealt. Players can swap their hand for 'The Miss' or drop out. 3. **Dealer's Swap**: If the dealer keeps their hand, they can swap one tile for the turn-up trump tile. 4. **Trick Play**: Lead any tile. Must follow suit (if lead is a 5-2, the suit is 5). If unable to follow, must play a trump if held.",
    keyRules: [
      'Suit of a tile is determined by its ends. A 5-2 belongs to suit 5 and suit 2.',
      'Trumps always beat non-trump suits.',
      'Only the first/second players to opt in can take the Miss.',
      'Each trick won earns 1/5 of the pool.',
      "Player who takes no tricks is 'Looed' and must pay penalty equal to original pool amount.",
    ],
